  "solution": "**Solution:**\n\nLet's calculate the average scores for each group over the given period (2014-2019) and determine which group has the highest average score.\n\n**Group 1: Board X - Boys**\n\n2014: 75.85%\n\n2015: 72.58%\n\n2016: 81.00%\n\n2017: 74.45%\n\n2018: 70.56%\n\n2019: 79.18%\n\n**Average for Board X - Boys:**\n\n {Average} = frac{{75.85 + 72.58 + 81.00 + 74.45 + 70.56 + 79.18}}{6} = (453.62)/(6) = 75.60\\% \n\n**Group 2: Board X - Girls**\n\n2014: 77.57%\n\n2015: 73.80%\n\n2016: 77.80%\n\n2017: 82.00%\n\n2018: 78.55%\n\n2019: 81.48%\n\n**Average for Board X - Girls:**\n\n {Average} = frac{{77.57 + 73.80 + 77.80 + 82.00 + 78.55 + 81.48}}{6} = (471.20)/(6) = 78.53\\% \n\n**Group 3: Board Y - Boys**\n\n2014: 74.56%\n\n2015: 69.68%\n\n2016: 68.50%\n\n2017: 77.56%\n\n2018: 70.50%\n\n2019: 73.55%\n\n**Average for Board Y - Boys:**\n\n{Average} = frac{{74.56 + 69.68 + 68.50 + 77.56 + 70.50 + 73.55}}{6} = (434.35)/(6) = 72.39\\% \n\n**Group 4: Board Y - Girls**\n\n2014: 76.65%\n\n2015: 71.45%\n\n2016: 70.45%\n\n2017: 80.67%\n\n2018: 76.78%\n\n2019: 81.65%\n\n**Average for Board Y - Girls:**\n\n {Average} = frac{{76.65 + 71.45 + 70.45 + 80.67 + 76.78 + 81.65}}{6} = (457.65)/(6) = 76.27\\% \n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe group with the highest average score is **Girls from Board X** with an average of 78.53%.\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option 3.**",
